From: Kevin Ellis <kevers@google.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:05:39 -0800
Subject: [M156] Fix UAF and cross-document lifecycle violation in keyframe
 snapshot

Original change's description:
> Fix UAF and cross-document lifecycle violation in keyframe snapshot
>
> The UAF was triggered due to the curve being destroyed mid-loop if
> resolving a style-dependent keyframe triggers a synchronous
> style/layout update that replaces or resets the curve. Resolved by
> holding a self-reference in CompositorAnimationCurve::UpdateKeyframeSnapshot.
>
> Addressing the UAF, revealed crash flakes due to lifecycle violations.
> The style and layout update is per document and the parent document
> is processed before the child. In the test, the slot reassignment
> in the child document was invalidating the parent's style.
>
> Flag guarded by the SyncCrossDocumentAnimationTiming killswitch:
>   - Synchronously update animation timing in Animation::SetOutdated()
>     when the effect target belongs to a different document than the
>     timeline, since servicing the target document's timelines will
>     not tick the animation.
>   - In KeyframeEffect::InvalidateEffectTargetStyle(), if the target
>     document is an ancestor of the animation or owning element's
>     document and is already style-clean (e.g., when a child frame's
>     style/layout pass cancels a CSS animation retargeted to the
>     parent document), defer SetNeedsAnimationStyleRecalc() to a
>     microtask so the parent document is not dirtied mid-lifecycle.
>   - Recalculate composited paint status for native paint worklet
>     animations directly in KeyframeEffect::DetachTarget() rather than
>     deferring to UpdateCompositedPaintStatus() during PreCommit.
>
